# 7. GROUP AND CHANNEL SUBMISSION SYSTEM

Users must be able to submit groups and channels without creating an account.

Create a modern submission page.

## Step 1: Select Submission Type

Options:

- WhatsApp Group.
- WhatsApp Channel.

## Step 2: Select Category

Display all active categories.

## Step 3: Enter WhatsApp Invite Link

Allow users to paste a valid WhatsApp invite link.

Examples of supported link formats may include:

- https://chat.whatsapp.com/...
- https://whatsapp.com/channel/...
- https://www.whatsapp.com/channel/...

Validate the URL server-side.

Reject unrelated URLs.

Do not accept arbitrary external URLs as WhatsApp invite links.

## Step 4: Automatic Metadata Fetching

This is a critical feature.

Implement the best available automatic metadata retrieval system for WhatsApp groups and channels.

When a user pastes a valid invite link:

1. Detect whether it is a group or channel.
2. Normalize the URL.
3. Attempt to retrieve the group/channel name.
4. Attempt to retrieve its profile picture.
5. Retrieve a description if a supported method provides one.
6. Display a live preview.
7. Allow the user to edit the name and description if needed.
8. Allow the user to upload a profile picture manually.

### Automatic Metadata Fetching Requirements

Do not assume WhatsApp provides a public API for fetching arbitrary group metadata.

Use a configurable metadata provider architecture.

Create a server-side metadata service with a provider interface.

Possible providers:

- Official or legitimately supported metadata integrations, where available.
- A configurable third-party metadata API.
- A manual fallback.

Provider API keys must be stored in environment variables.

Never expose provider API keys in frontend JavaScript.

Do not use a user's personal WhatsApp credentials.

Do not require a user to scan a QR code or connect their private WhatsApp account.

Do not use unauthorized private WhatsApp endpoints.

Do not scrape private group data.

Do not claim that metadata was successfully fetched when it was not.

If automatic fetching fails:

Display a clear message:

"We couldn't automatically retrieve this group's information. Please enter the group name and upload its profile picture."

Provide:

- Group name input.
- Description input.
- Image upload.
- Preview.

The user should still be able to submit the link.

### Metadata Caching

Cache successfully retrieved metadata.

Use a database table or caching mechanism.

Avoid fetching the same link repeatedly.

Use reasonable expiration times.

### Profile Picture Handling

Use Supabase Storage for uploaded images.

Validate image file types.

Validate image size.

Do not trust image URLs submitted by users.

Avoid allowing arbitrary external image URLs to create server-side request forgery risks.

